cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in academic work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "NDN Web Animation: a conceptual study of NDN forwarding strategies in wireless multi-hop networks"
abstract: >-
  A backend-free web animation that shows how the stock NDN forwarding
  strategies (best-route, ASF, multicast and self-learning) behave on a small
  wireless multi-hop topology with redundant paths, two consumers and one
  producer. A seeded discrete-event simulator mirrors the forwarding rules of
  NFD and the hello and routing timers of NLSR, and counts packets delivered
  by the producer or by caches, lost and repeated. It is the conceptual
  groundwork for a new forwarding strategy.
